  "id": "sensory-deficit",
  "term": "sensory deficit",
  "definition": "A sensory deficit is a reduction or impairment in the functioning of a sense, such as vision impairment. In psychology and social functioning, this kind of sensory decline can disrupt autonomy, emotional regulation, and social participation, which may increase vulnerability to depressive symptoms.",
